  26: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  27:     """
  28:     Double the canvas, copy the input on the main diagonal, and draw green separator rows through each vertical gap.
  29: 
  30:     Input structure
  31:     The background is black. All foreground pixels form one or more identical
  32:     non-background row pairs separated by a blank row.
  33: 
  34:     Rule
  35:     Build a 2H x 2W black canvas, paste the input into the upper-left and
  36:     lower-right H x W blocks, and color the blank row between each paired row
  37:     green across the full output width in both diagonal copies.
  38: 
  39:     Key insight
  40:     The foreground marks horizontal separator rows by bracketing each gap with
  41:     matching rows; the whole pattern is then repeated on the diagonal.
